00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:49.280
- Right, so I direct the Emory
Healthcare Veterans Program.

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:52.900
We are funded by
philanthropy in a large grant

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:54.710
from the Wounded Warrior Project,

00:13:54.710 --> 00:13:57.980
so many, many thanks to WWP.

00:13:57.980 --> 00:14:02.890
We can bring in Post-9/11 veterans

00:14:02.890 --> 00:14:04.680
from all around the country.

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:07.560
We bring them into our place in Atlanta,

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:10.330
set them up in a hotel near our clinic,

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:13.050
and we give them a lot
of treatment every day,

00:14:13.050 --> 00:14:17.380
for two weeks, it's called an
Intensive Outpatient Program.

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:19.610
They get a lot of individual therapy,

00:14:19.610 --> 00:14:22.060
we do evidence-based therapy,

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:24.920
so that's therapy that
has been shown in studies

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:26.670
to be helpful.

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:30.390
We treat PTSD, depression, anxiety,

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:35.320
we've got specific tracks
for substance use or misuse,

00:14:35.320 --> 00:14:39.790
we've got a track for mild
traumatic brain injury,

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:43.070
we've got interventions for pain,

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:47.460
we teach everybody yoga, they
can have acupuncture for pain.

00:14:47.460 --> 00:14:51.870
So we've got family
surfaces, even before COVID.

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:54.430
We involved the family via telemedicine,

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:55.540
'cause we really want people

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:58.990
to eat, breathe and sleep the
program while they're here,

00:14:58.990 --> 00:15:02.490
but we involve the
family via telemedicine.

00:15:02.490 --> 00:15:05.910
And we, everything is at
no cost to the veteran,

00:15:05.910 --> 00:15:08.530
so transportation, housing.

00:15:08.530 --> 00:15:10.300
They get more therapy in two weeks

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:13.290
than most people get in an entire year

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:14.900
and it's effective therapy.

00:15:14.900 --> 00:15:18.390
So I don't know if people
know there's a lot of dropout

00:15:18.390 --> 00:15:19.543
from PTSD treatment.

00:15:19.543 --> 00:15:22.497
I mean, PTSD is a disorder of avoidance

00:15:22.497 --> 00:15:24.530
and that means therapy too.

00:15:24.530 --> 00:15:27.575
We have a 93% completion rate.

00:15:27.575 --> 00:15:28.410
- Wow.

00:15:28.410 --> 00:15:31.580
- So I really, I've been
treating PTSD my entire career,

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:34.110
I think this is the way
to treat it, with the IOP.

00:15:34.110 --> 00:15:36.920
So every Monday we've got
a new cohort of veterans.

00:15:36.920 --> 00:15:38.580
It's a two week program,

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:39.780
so any given time,

00:15:39.780 --> 00:15:41.410
we've got people that
it's their first week

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:42.660
and their second week.

00:15:42.660 --> 00:15:44.530
So they've got a cohort of veterans

00:15:44.530 --> 00:15:46.540
who are also doing the hard work

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:48.540
